{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790759-horror-focused-hunter-groups","id":790759,"title":"Horror focused hunter groups?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-22T02:07:22-08:00","id":790759,"title":"Horror focused hunter groups?","content":"So with the inclusion of horrors in chronicles of darkness, I got to thinking- I would assume that the horrors in their infinite variety are quite likely the most numerous type of monster.<br /> <br /> Anyone come up with a hunter compact or conspiracy that focuses not one of the big groups in the cofd, but the numerous weird things that go bump in the night?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T03:57:31-08:00","id":790790,"title":"","content":"Do not Horrors are just a mechanical name for the monsters? Did not read their section in corebook yet, but they seem to be Yeti. Mothman, Chupacabra, Jersey Devil and all weird beings not connected to supernatural splats themselves...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T19:08:44-08:00","id":791217,"title":"","content":"Horrors aren't a grouping of anything. They're the monsters that fall in between the broad categorical cracks, and don't have very good explanations behind them. Their whole purpose is to be one-off oddities that don't tie into the larger World of Darkness. <br /> <br /> Making a group based around them defeats the purpose; Horrors are the shit they deal with every day, and have to wonder &quot;what the fuck was that?&quot; about for the rest of their lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T07:38:40-08:00","id":791574,"title":"","content":"The only angle I can see for a compact devoted exclusively to horrors would be some kind of support organization devoted to analyzing these things and creating a database for other hunters to use. Thing is, that seems like it would fall pretty easily under Network Zero's purview.<br /> <br /> I could, however, see a monster-of-the-week style chronicle that purely pits the PCs against a barrage of horrors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T22:14:54-08:00","id":830829,"title":"","content":"In reality, Horrors are mostly what our real world calls <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cryptid\" target=\"_blank\">Cryptids</a>. And cryptids is all way <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Null Mysteriis</span></span></i> field, with capturing, analyzing and proving that they are <b>real</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-16-2016, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T07:30:30-08:00","id":831013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790759-horror-focused-hunter-groups?p=791574#post791574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only angle I can see for a compact devoted exclusively to horrors would be some kind of support organization devoted to analyzing these things and creating a database for other hunters to use. Thing is, that seems like it would fall pretty easily under Network Zero's purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>The occasional takes on a compact based on the way hunters work in Supernatural would seem to be appropriate too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T07:46:23-08:00","id":831022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790759-horror-focused-hunter-groups#post790759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So with the inclusion of horrors in chronicles of darkness, I got to thinking- I would assume that the horrors in their infinite variety are quite likely the most numerous type of monster.<br /> <br /> Anyone come up with a hunter compact or conspiracy that focuses not one of the big groups in the cofd, but the numerous weird things that go bump in the night?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My hope is that the Horror creation rules will be repeated in the 2nd ed Hunter book with additional example Horrors, including Horror versions of vampires, werewolves, and mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}